      "text": "do not your alms before men, to be seen of them, Matt. 6:1 (3 Ne. 13:1). appear not unto men to fast, Matt. 6:18 (3 Ne. 13:18). evil things come from within, and defile the man, Mark 7:23. out of the good treasure of his heart bringeth forth … good, Luke 6:45. pray God … the thought of thine heart may be forgiven, Acts 8:22. to him that esteemeth any thing to be unclean, to him it is unclean, Rom. 14:14. take heed lest … this liberty of yours become a stumblingblock, 1 Cor. 8:9. bringing … every thought to the obedience of Christ, 2 Cor. 10:5. if there be any praise, think on these things, Philip. 4:8. discerner of the thoughts and intents of the heart, Heb. 4:12. hospitality … without grudging, 1 Pet. 4:9. every man that hath this hope in him purifieth himself, 1 Jn. 3:3.",
